\title{API Reference}

\p{
  \code{import baux} lazily loads functional state transitions, pipeline stages, parameter domain specifications, and standalone Epistemic Nearest Neighbor (\code{ENN}) surrogates. Across all entrypoints, flat input arrays \code{x} have shape \code{(N, D)} (\code{float64}) inside natural domain bounds \code{[low, high]}, and objective arrays \code{y} (maximization convention) and optional observation variances \code{y_var} have shape \code{(N,)} for scalar targets or \code{(N, M)} (\code{float64}) for multi-output targets. Functional entrypoints (\code{baux.init}, \code{baux.ask}, \code{baux.tell}, \code{baux.enn_init}, \code{baux.enn_append}) take and return immutable state objects ([\code{OptimizerState}](#baux.OptimizerState), [\code{ENNState}](#baux.ENNState)) whose array properties return read-only views (\code{writeable=False}), while [\code{Optimizer}](#baux.Optimizer) and [\code{ENN}](#baux.ENN) wrap the same solver in stateful classes.
}

\<div>[id]{baux-api-filter}{}

